      {
        "review_id": 837764281,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r837764281-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Fascinating--must see!",
        "text": "I was not sure if I would enjoy visiting a site dedicated to cremations, but it turned out to be fascinating.  This UNESCO sight on the banks of the Bagmati River is a Hindu temple dedicated to Lord Shiva.  This is where people come to cremate their dead.  Funeral pyres for the line the banks, and it was really a cultural experience.  You will even see people burning shrouds only, which means the person who passed away is not in Kathmandu and they do not have the body there.\n\nBe sure to climb higher and higher, where you can take in the entire complex from above.  It is truly visual overload--you won't know where to look first.  Because the property is so large, it will not feel crowded.\n\nA must-see while you are in Kathmandu.",
